  "datasheet": "https://documentation.espressif.com/esp32-c3_datasheet_en.pdf",
  "verified": true,
  "summary": "Espressif entry-level RISC-V ESP32-C3 board with an ESP32-C3-MINI-1(U) module (4 MB in-package flash), Micro-USB via USB-to-UART bridge, and an RGB LED on GPIO8.",
  "warnings": [
    {
      "level": "danger",
      "text": "3.3 V logic only. The GPIOs are not 5 V tolerant; never connect a 5 V signal to them."
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "text": "Strapping pins GPIO2, GPIO8 and GPIO9 are read at reset. GPIO9 low = download mode; GPIO8 must be high for download mode and also drives the RGB LED; GPIO2 should be high. External pull-ups/pull-downs on them can stop the board from booting.",
      "pins": [
        "J1-4",
        "J3-6",
        "J3-5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "GPIO18/GPIO19 are the native USB D-/D+ (USB Serial/JTAG). GPIO20/GPIO21 are UART0, wired to the USB-to-UART bridge used by the Micro-USB port.",
      "pins": [
        "J3-13",
        "J3-14",
        "J3-3",
        "J3-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "Only GPIO0-4 have factory-calibrated ADC1 channels. ADC2 (GPIO5) is not factory-calibrated and does not work on some chip revisions (datasheet).",
      "pins": [
        "J3-10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "text": "GPIO4-7 are the pin JTAG interface (MTMS, MTDI, MTCK, MTDO). They are free if you debug over USB Serial/JTAG.",
      "pins": [
        "J3-11",
        "J3-10",
        "J3-9",
        "J3-8"
      ]
    }
  ],
